WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.206
<i> NARRATOR: What will you
 do when calamity strikes?</i>

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:12.846
<i> A survival situation may
 be unlikely for humans,</i>

00:00:14.713 --> 00:00:16.682
<i> but for animals in the wild,</i>

00:00:16.715 --> 00:00:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> preparing for
 disaster is their day job.</i>

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Good planning can
 mean the difference
 between life and death.</i>

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.994
<i>From cutting edge engineering,</i>

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:31.164
<i>to elaborate escape strategies.</i>

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:36.135
<i> We're taking notes on how
 these animals prepare for</i>

00:00:36.168 --> 00:00:39.906
<i> emergency situations, in
 the world's weirdest ways.</i>

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:45.211
<i> When faced with chaos,
 the greatest weapon,</i>

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:47.747
<i> is a plan.</i>

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:52.652
(theme music plays)

00:00:56.388 --> 00:00:59.059
<i> Winter in North America.</i>

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:02.395 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Like a scene from
 the end of the world.</i>

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:05.331
<i> Food is scarce.</i>

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.768 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> And with hungry
 raiders on the prowl,</i>

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> getting caught out
 in the open can mean,</i>

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:14.741
<i> a grisly end.</i>

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:22.048 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> But in this frozen wasteland,
 a fortress stands defiant.</i>

00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:28.688
<i> Steam rises from its chimney.</i>

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.859
<i> Something inside, is alive.</i>

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.597
<i> What could have built,
 this emergency bunker?</i>

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:46.573
<i> Just a few months before
 the onslaught of winter,</i>

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:51.077 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> the forest is
 abuzz with activity.</i>

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:59.152
<i> It's not chainsaws,
 but jaws at work.</i>

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:05.859
<i> The American beaver.</i>

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:11.030 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> These plant eating
 rodents may seem docile,</i>

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:13.733 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> but they're about to
 transform their habitat,</i>

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> in an extraordinary
 animal renovation project!</i>

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:22.342 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Phase one,
 collecting building material.</i>

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:26.212 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> Beavers have
 four iron-infused,</i>

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:29.348
<i> chisel-sharp incisors that
 keep growing all throughout</i>

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:31.417
<i> their lives and
 never wear out.</i>

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.956 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> They can munch their
 way through a small tree,</i>

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:40.226
<i> six inches thick, in
 a matter of minutes.</i>

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Next, they'll need to
 transport the wood to the</i>

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:49.502 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> construction site, but
 no trucks or cranes here.</i>

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:57.777
<i> Beavers use canal highways
 to float their cargo home.</i>

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:02.215 align:start position:0%
<i>Their paddle tails and
duck-like feet can propel them</i>

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.284
<i> through water at up
 to five miles an hour!</i>

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:11.724
<i> And now, they execute phase
 two of their bunker project;</i>

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.028
<i> the beaver dam.</i>

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:20.300 align:start position:0%
<i>The trickling sound of leaking
water triggers one of the
beaver's strongest instincts.</i>

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.571
<i> Build, build, build!</i>

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:29.141 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> This creates a
 large defensive moat,</i>

00:03:29.174 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start position:0%
<i>in which they construct the
final phase: the beaver lodge.</i>

00:03:37.182 --> 00:03:40.453
<i> They pile up rocks, branches
 and logs as high as six feet</i>

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:44.857
<i> above the water, and weather
 seal the structure with mud.</i>

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:51.297
<i> They'll need to work fast:
 autumn is about to end.</i>

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:58.171
<i> But the best laid plans, can
 attract unwanted attention.</i>

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:03.343 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> The beavers have
 been stocking up twigs
 and branches underwater.</i>

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.379
<i> Food to last through winter.</i>

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:10.283 align:start position:0%
<i>And this hulking moose is
just reaping all the benefits.</i>

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.620
<i> No plan and no permission.</i>

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:17.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> But how do you
 stop someone almost
 30 times your body weight?</i>

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.996 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> The beaver's paddle
 tail makes a loud splash.</i>

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:26.532
<i> A stern warning, and also an
 alarm call for other beavers.</i>

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.876 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Size doesn't matter,
 when you've got attitude.</i>

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.185
<i> The beaver lodge is complete,</i>

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:48.755 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> in time for the
 late November snow.</i>

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:54.327
<i> This astonishing structure
 is more than just a shelter,</i>

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:58.831 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> it's got secure
 underwater entrances,</i>

00:05:00.165 --> 00:05:02.702 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> multiple rooms, and
 even a ventilation shaft.</i>

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.740 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> And now that the mud
 walls have frozen solid,</i>

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.943 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> this bunker is
 virtually impenetrable.</i>

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:19.518 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> These little emergency
 planners may have created the</i>

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:22.588
<i> safest place to ride out
 the winter armageddon.</i>

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:29.529
<i>It's certainly not easy to build
a survival hideout from scratch,</i>

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:32.965
<i> so what if you didn't need to?</i>

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:41.541
<i> The warm waters of
 the indo-pacific.</i>

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:48.781
<i> This is an unforgiving
 fish-eat-fish world.</i>

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:54.420
<i> Apex predators are on patrol,</i>

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.657 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> and deadly traps
 are ready to spring.</i>

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:03.296 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> If you're a small
 fish in this big pond,</i>

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:05.732 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> it's probably
 going to end in teeth.</i>

00:06:13.672 --> 00:06:15.274 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> These colorful
 clownfish, however,</i>

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:17.977 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> have discovered an
 unusual place to bunker down;</i>

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:22.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> among the stinging
 tentacles of a sea anemone.</i>

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:29.856
<i> There are over 1,000 species
 of sea anemone in the ocean.</i>

00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:37.229 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> But don't be fooled, they
 are nothing like the innocent</i>

00:06:37.262 --> 00:06:39.332
<i> flowers they're named after.</i>

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:44.604 align:start position:0%
<i>Sea anemones are
meat-eating killer fish traps!</i>

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:49.108
<i> With the slightest touch,</i>

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:55.214 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> it injects a venomous
 neurotoxin into its prey,</i>

00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:58.050 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> strong enough
 to paralyze a small fish.</i>

00:07:00.452 --> 00:07:04.089 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> The tentacles drag
 the helpless fish
 into its central mouth,</i>

00:07:04.122 --> 00:07:06.692
<i> where it's digested whole!</i>

00:07:10.762 --> 00:07:13.166
<i> They may be clownfish,
 but they're no clowns.</i>

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:18.271 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Sheltering in the arms
 of a predator takes a
 special kind of preparation.</i>

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:23.642
<i> Scientists believe that
 clownfish brush themselves</i>

00:07:23.675 --> 00:07:25.511 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> carefully against</i> 
<i> the tentacles,</i>

00:07:25.911 --> 00:07:28.281
<i> until a layer of anemone
 mucous covers the fish.</i>

00:07:30.782 --> 00:07:33.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> This fools the
 anemone into accepting it.</i>

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:38.925 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Clownfish aren't the only
 ones to befriend this killer.</i>

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:44.263
<i> Smaller sea anemones are a
 hot commodity in the field</i>

00:07:44.296 --> 00:07:45.998
<i> of underwater security.</i>

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:51.204 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> As part of the hermit
 crab's bizarre survival plan,</i>

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:55.641 align:start position:0%
<i>it gathers up sea
anemones to use as bodyguards.</i>

00:07:58.076 --> 00:08:01.046 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Hermit crabs don't
 have armor of their own,</i>

00:08:01.079 --> 00:08:03.883
<i> so they hide out in shells
 discarded by other animals.</i>

00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:07.953 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> And this one's
 got a sea anemone,</i>

00:08:07.986 --> 00:08:09.989
<i> pre-installed!</i>

00:08:16.194 --> 00:08:18.498
<i> But one isn't always enough.</i>

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:22.969
<i>Sea anemones like staying put.</i>

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:26.439
<i> They grip on to hard surfaces
 with a large disc-like foot.</i>

00:08:27.739 --> 00:08:30.476 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> This hermit crab
 knows just the trick.</i>

00:08:32.844 --> 00:08:35.515 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> A slight tickle here,
 an easy lift.</i>

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:41.387
<i>His moves are so smooth that
the anemone doesn't even close</i>

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:44.490
<i> up during the procedure.</i>

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:53.866 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> An octopus has
 spotted his prey.</i>

00:08:57.402 --> 00:09:02.108
<i> He pounces on the crab, but
 gets a mouthful of anemone.</i>

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:07.013
<i> He tries again.</i>

00:09:12.618 --> 00:09:14.954
<i> The meal is striking back.</i>

00:09:15.954 --> 00:09:19.458
<i> It's not worth his trouble.</i>

00:09:19.491 --> 00:09:24.397 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> And the hermit
 crab's mobile fortress
 is a stinging success.</i>

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:32.905 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: You may have
 think you've seen weird,</i>

00:09:32.938 --> 00:09:36.609 line:0%
<i> but things get even weirder
 when sea anemones go to war,</i>

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.378
<i> with each other.</i>

00:09:40.245 --> 00:09:43.115 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> That's because two
 families struggle to
 share a single boulder.</i>

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:49.855
<i> The science of genetics has
 taught us that the need to</i>

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:54.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> protect and spread
 DNA is a basic
 driver of animal behavior.</i>

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:02.034 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> The aggregating sea anemone of
 the Pacific U.S. coast has</i>

00:10:02.067 --> 00:10:04.337
<i> taken that to extremes.</i>

00:10:07.706 --> 00:10:11.110
<i> It can reproduce sexually by
 releasing sperm and eggs into</i>

00:10:11.143 --> 00:10:13.913
<i> the sea to drift and mingle.</i>

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:19.485 align:start position:0%
<i>But weirdly they also multiply
by cloning themselves;</i>

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:22.388
<i> splitting in half
 like dividing cells.</i>

00:10:24.423 --> 00:10:27.393 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Through cloning they can
 rapidly colonize every nearby</i>

00:10:27.426 --> 00:10:30.863 align:start position:0%
<i>space with genetically
identical copies of themselves.</i>

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:38.270
<i>The more crowded their living
conditions the better they are</i>

00:10:38.303 --> 00:10:41.707 align:start position:0%
<i>able to withstand the constant
daily drought they face
during low tide.</i>

00:10:44.476 --> 00:10:47.613
<i>And by cloning each anemone,
they ensure that its territory</i>

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:50.716
<i> is dominated only
 by its own DNA.</i>

00:10:54.152 --> 00:10:57.322
<i> Until two growing colonies
 of assembled anemones come</i>

00:10:57.355 --> 00:10:59.625
<i> tentacle to tentacle.</i>

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:05.731 align:start position:0%
<i>The two colonies are the same
species but carry different DNA.</i>

00:11:07.999 --> 00:11:11.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> They're in a permanent
 war of attrition for
 possession of this boulder.</i>

00:11:14.072 --> 00:11:16.542
<i> The anemone clones on the
 front lines of this war have</i>

00:11:16.575 --> 00:11:21.346
<i> developed stinging clubs,
 which they use to fight off</i>

00:11:21.379 --> 00:11:23.582
<i> the advancing enemy anemone.</i>

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:28.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> The warrior clones on
 the battlefront can
 die from repeated strikes.</i>

00:11:30.322 --> 00:11:32.124
<i> Or do they?</i>

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:35.494
<i> Each animal in this army is
 genetically the same animal,</i>

00:11:36.561 --> 00:11:41.801
<i> so weirdly; they can die,
 yet still live on in others.</i>

00:11:42.101 --> 00:11:45.004
<i> So the clone war goes on.</i>

00:11:47.639 --> 00:11:51.043
<i> Lungfish are an ancient fish
 that can be found in Africa,</i>

00:11:51.076 --> 00:11:53.279
<i> South America and Australia.</i>

00:11:54.013 --> 00:11:57.683 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> They live in the murky
 margins of swamps and rivers.</i>

00:12:03.288 --> 00:12:06.358
<i> But sometimes, water can
 dry up during droughts.</i>

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:10.763 align:start position:0%
<i>Lungfish have found a way
around this fundamental problem.</i>

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:15.601
<i> Their strange mutation has
 enabled them to survive for</i>

00:12:15.634 --> 00:12:18.671
<i> more than 300 million years.</i>

00:12:20.405 --> 00:12:23.109 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> When their
 watery home vanishes;</i>

00:12:23.342 --> 00:12:26.112 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> lungfish turn to
 breathing air like a mammal.</i>

00:12:32.818 --> 00:12:35.721
<i> Droughts can last
 for years on end.</i>

00:12:38.356 --> 00:12:41.527
<i> So the lungfish digs down
 in mud to create a burrow.</i>

00:12:44.563 --> 00:12:47.199 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> Where it coats
 itself in mucous,</i>

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.736
<i> which dries to a
 leathery body-bag,</i>

00:12:50.769 --> 00:12:53.739
<i> protecting it from
 total dehydration.</i>

00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:59.745
<i> The lungfish then shuts
 its system down and waits.</i>

00:13:07.385 --> 00:13:10.156
<i> It can survive for years
 if that's what it takes.</i>

00:13:12.991 --> 00:13:15.994
<i> The lake and the fish
 may be long forgotten,</i>

00:13:16.027 --> 00:13:18.297 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> but the lungfish
 will still be there.</i>

00:13:22.467 --> 00:13:25.704 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> Its metabolic
 rate drops by 60%.</i>

00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:29.141 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> What little
 energy it does need,</i>

00:13:29.374 --> 00:13:32.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> comes from slowly
 consuming its own muscles.</i>

00:13:32.978 --> 00:13:35.648
<i> It effectively eats
 itself to survive.</i>

00:13:40.585 --> 00:13:43.655 align:start position:0%
<i>When the drought
breaking deluge finally comes,</i>

00:13:43.688 --> 00:13:46.458 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> the lungfish awakens
 from its dormant state,</i>

00:13:46.491 --> 00:13:48.894
<i>re-animated and ready to roll.</i>

00:14:03.208 --> 00:14:06.312
<i> On an evolutionary scale,
 this was a game changer,</i>

00:14:07.479 --> 00:14:10.916 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> that's kept the lungfish
 alive since before dinosaurs.</i>

00:14:17.255 --> 00:14:19.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Some weird animals have
 developed battle plans that</i>

00:14:19.724 --> 00:14:23.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> can defeat the enemy,
 without even touching them.</i>

00:14:25.964 --> 00:14:29.501 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> The dry, red earth of
 Africa's Kalahari desert.</i>

00:14:34.239 --> 00:14:37.643 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Meerkats have banded together
 in a tribal community.</i>

00:14:39.778 --> 00:14:42.248
<i> While the mob turns up the
 dirt in search of breakfast,</i>

00:14:45.283 --> 00:14:48.487 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> one adult takes on
 the critical role, of sentry.</i>

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:54.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> He stands upright on the
 highest lookout for over an</i>

00:14:54.726 --> 00:14:59.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> hour at a time, where
 he can spot predators from
 more than half a mile away.</i>

00:15:01.633 --> 00:15:04.870 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> His persistent
 call reassures the
 gang that the coast is clear.</i>

00:15:08.106 --> 00:15:10.876
<i> But at the first
 sign of danger,</i>

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:15.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> he uses one of 30 distinct
 messages to warn his
 family of the threat.</i>

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.953
(alarm call)

00:15:23.421 --> 00:15:25.958
<i> This time, it's a cape cobra.</i>

00:15:25.991 --> 00:15:28.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Among the most
 dangerous snakes in Africa.</i>

00:15:29.027 --> 00:15:30.495
<i> With venom so potent,</i>

00:15:30.528 --> 00:15:33.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> it could kill a grown
 man in 30 minutes.</i>

00:15:36.101 --> 00:15:39.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Many creatures would run
 from this deadly adversary.</i>

00:15:39.705 --> 00:15:42.741
<i> But not the meerkats,
 they stand their ground.</i>

00:15:44.209 --> 00:15:45.911
<i> They've got a plan.</i>

00:15:50.749 --> 00:15:53.786
<i> For the meerkats,
 the best fight,</i>

00:15:53.986 --> 00:15:55.955
<i> is no fight at all.</i>

00:15:58.656 --> 00:16:00.625 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> They dart their
 heads back and forth,</i>

00:16:00.658 --> 00:16:03.128
<i> spit and growl menacingly.</i>

00:16:03.728 --> 00:16:06.231 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> It's an elaborate
 intimidation display,</i>

00:16:06.264 --> 00:16:08.667 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> a bluff to
 discourage the snake.</i>

00:16:10.435 --> 00:16:13.906
<i>But there's more to this plan.</i>

00:16:15.607 --> 00:16:18.544
<i> Multiple moving targets
 can confuse the predator.</i>

00:16:19.511 --> 00:16:22.181 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> The snake has
 difficulty singling out
 and attacking its prey.</i>

00:16:28.586 --> 00:16:31.056
<i> It's all too much
 for the cape cobra,</i>

00:16:33.892 --> 00:16:36.929 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> and it makes a
 tactical retreat.</i>

00:16:38.963 --> 00:16:43.268
<i> The meerkat mafia have made
 an offer it can't refuse.</i>

00:16:44.669 --> 00:16:48.007 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> You mess with one, you
 mess with all of the family.</i>

00:16:53.111 --> 00:16:55.714 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: We've seen
 the most amazing defenses:</i>

00:16:56.314 --> 00:16:58.650 line:0%
<i> playing dress-up,</i>

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:02.721
<i>playing house, playing offense.</i>

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:08.226
<i> But this weaverbird has a
 different kind of defense</i>

00:17:08.259 --> 00:17:10.763
<i> strategy to avoid predators:</i>

00:17:11.063 --> 00:17:13.632
<i> an excellent home
 security system.</i>

00:17:14.432 --> 00:17:16.902 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Of course, as with
 any good real estate,</i>

00:17:16.935 --> 00:17:19.071
<i> it's all about location.</i>

00:17:20.072 --> 00:17:22.541 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> He's found an
 acacia tree with
 everything a potential</i>

00:17:22.574 --> 00:17:26.912 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> mate could want;
 a water view, shade,</i>

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:32.451 align:start position:0%
<i>and most importantly,
viciously sharp thorns to keep</i>

00:17:32.484 --> 00:17:34.319
<i> most predators away.</i>

00:17:37.655 --> 00:17:40.092
<i> The custom built home
 doesn't hurt either.</i>

00:17:42.794 --> 00:17:45.964 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Male weavers build intricate,
 tightly woven nests.</i>

00:17:52.871 --> 00:17:56.141 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> If the female is
 happy with her
 general contractor's design,</i>

00:17:59.277 --> 00:18:01.547
<i> she moves in.</i>

00:18:05.316 --> 00:18:07.552
<i> Weavers depend upon their
 construction skills to keep</i>

00:18:07.585 --> 00:18:10.222
<i> their hatchlings safe.</i>

00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:16.862
<i> Usually, it works.</i>

00:18:19.864 --> 00:18:23.168
<i> But it doesn't stop the
 predators from trying.</i>

00:18:26.804 --> 00:18:30.309 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> The noisy, boisterous
 colony is attracting some
 unwanted attention.</i>

00:18:33.444 --> 00:18:36.548 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> This snake wants
 eggs for breakfast.</i>

00:18:39.317 --> 00:18:42.821 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> As it carefully
 winds its way around the
 thorns towards a nest,</i>

00:18:45.023 --> 00:18:46.992
<i> a weaver sounds
 the burglar alarm.</i>

00:18:47.225 --> 00:18:50.162
(chirping)

00:18:50.629 --> 00:18:54.199
<i> With a few deft moves,
 the weaver dumps his
 nemesis into the drink.</i>

00:19:02.507 --> 00:19:05.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Fending off this
 attacker won't be so easy.</i>

00:19:07.912 --> 00:19:11.150
<i> The gabar goshawk can
 perch right on the nest.</i>

00:19:11.617 --> 00:19:14.219
<i> Actually breaking into
 it is a little harder.</i>

00:19:18.489 --> 00:19:24.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> But all it takes is
 one little design flaw and
 the hatchlings are toast.</i>

00:19:32.303 --> 00:19:34.573 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> Even with all
 their precautions,</i>

00:19:35.073 --> 00:19:36.274
<i> for the weavers,</i>

00:19:36.307 --> 00:19:39.511
<i> this is still a pretty
 dangerous neighborhood.</i>

00:19:40.712 --> 00:19:42.914
<i> The weaver bird's weird look
 out call takes the passive</i>

00:19:42.947 --> 00:19:45.217
<i> approach to survival.</i>

00:19:45.417 --> 00:19:47.953
<i> But when your enemy is
 mother nature herself,</i>

00:19:47.986 --> 00:19:50.789
<i> the best defense of all
 is to get out of town.</i>

00:19:54.192 --> 00:19:56.728
<i>Deep in the amazon rainforest,</i>

00:19:58.029 --> 00:20:01.233
<i> the ground is ablaze
 with the tiny terror,</i>

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:03.669
<i> of the fire ant.</i>

00:20:04.302 --> 00:20:06.304
<i> A torrent of soldiers!</i>

00:20:06.337 --> 00:20:08.974
<i> Armed to the teeth
 with a burning bite,</i>

00:20:09.007 --> 00:20:11.977 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> they strip
 animals to the bone.</i>

00:20:18.549 --> 00:20:21.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Its sting contains
 cell-destroying venom that</i>

00:20:21.219 --> 00:20:23.388
<i> wreaks havoc on
 even human flesh.</i>

00:20:29.894 --> 00:20:34.065
<i> This flaming horde of
 ants seems unstoppable.</i>

00:20:34.098 --> 00:20:36.635 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> But when the
 rainy season comes,</i>

00:20:40.104 --> 00:20:43.709
<i> the amazon brings out
 nature's extinguisher:</i>

00:20:47.011 --> 00:20:50.415 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> an epic flood of
 biblical proportions!</i>

00:20:51.382 --> 00:20:55.053
<i> Over 100,000 square miles
 of forest submerged under</i>

00:20:55.086 --> 00:20:57.990
<i> some 40 feet of water.</i>

00:20:59.424 --> 00:21:02.894
<i> The end is surely nigh.</i>

00:21:06.831 --> 00:21:10.002 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> But not even water can
 douse this ingenious inferno!</i>

00:21:16.174 --> 00:21:18.043
<i> The ants join together.</i>

00:21:18.076 --> 00:21:22.214 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Their bodies combine
 to form an incredible,
 floating ark!</i>

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:34.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> They trap tiny bubbles
 of air around themselves
 to increase their buoyancy.</i>

00:21:34.592 --> 00:21:38.597 align:start position:0%
<i>This miraculous raft can
stay afloat for months on end.</i>

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:42.534
<i> But the journey is
 fraught with peril.</i>

00:21:45.002 --> 00:21:48.406 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Their most precious
 cargo is the colony's queen.</i>

00:21:48.439 --> 00:21:50.842 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Their future
 depends on her survival,</i>

00:21:51.275 --> 00:21:53.144
<i> so she stays dry,</i>

00:21:53.177 --> 00:21:56.014
<i> literally trampling on
 her royal subjects.</i>

00:21:58.383 --> 00:22:01.119
<i> The lower peasants are
 picked off one by one,</i>

00:22:01.152 --> 00:22:04.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> like floating
 clumps of fish food.</i>

00:22:05.556 --> 00:22:07.492
<i> Some will drown.</i>

00:22:07.525 --> 00:22:10.595
<i> But she's a queen to die for!</i>

00:22:13.898 --> 00:22:16.401
<i> Finally, landfall.</i>

00:22:17.869 --> 00:22:20.372
<i> The ants haul 'her
 highness' to safety.</i>

00:22:20.405 --> 00:22:24.443 align:start position:0%
<i>The dynasty has found salvation
on their self-made ark.</i>

00:22:26.010 --> 00:22:28.480
<i> And now they return
 to what they do best:</i>

00:22:28.513 --> 00:22:30.649
<i> spreading their wildfire.</i>

00:22:33.017 --> 00:22:35.687 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Even against a
 catastrophic emergency,</i>

00:22:35.720 --> 00:22:38.924
<i> the fire ants blaze on.</i>

00:22:48.266 --> 00:22:50.869 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Getting a move on is a
 well-known survival strategy.</i>

00:22:51.436 --> 00:22:55.440 align:start position:0%
<i>For mother turtles, her
journey is all about going home.</i>

00:22:56.474 --> 00:22:59.677
<i> She often gets credit
 for being a good mother.</i>

00:22:59.710 --> 00:23:03.048 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> But really, she's
 just a good navigator.</i>

00:23:03.581 --> 00:23:07.085
<i> Seven different species
 roam the world's oceans.</i>

00:23:08.152 --> 00:23:11.156
<i>When it's time to have babies,
mothers are famous for finding</i>

00:23:11.189 --> 00:23:14.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> their way back to the
 exact place they were born.</i>

00:23:16.227 --> 00:23:18.830
<i> One turtle with a satellite
 tag was recorded making a</i>

00:23:18.863 --> 00:23:22.367
<i> journey of over 12,000 miles.</i>

00:23:22.934 --> 00:23:26.938
<i> That kind of painstaking
 precision is only for
 getting to the beach.</i>

00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:32.577
<i> Once they arrive, it's
 chaos: a fin- flapping,</i>

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:34.846
<i> sand-kicking free for all.</i>

00:23:36.347 --> 00:23:39.117 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> This mother green turtle
 may dig several nests and lay</i>

00:23:39.150 --> 00:23:41.386
<i> multiple clutches of
 eggs over a season.</i>

00:23:43.287 --> 00:23:45.457
<i> She can navigate the globe.</i>

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:48.059 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> But can't quite remember
 where she dug her last nest.</i>

00:23:50.595 --> 00:23:53.331
<i>The eggs she accidentally digs
up tonight could even be the</i>

00:23:53.364 --> 00:23:55.734
<i> ones she laid last month.</i>

00:23:59.670 --> 00:24:03.208 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> The morning sun
 bakes them to a crisp.</i>

00:24:03.975 --> 00:24:05.777
<i> As the season wears on,</i>

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:08.613 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> mother turtles
 continue to arrive.</i>

00:24:08.813 --> 00:24:12.250 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Eggs begin to hatch even
 as mothers are still nesting.</i>

00:24:14.085 --> 00:24:18.690
<i> Once again, mom doesn't
 seem to notice or care.</i>

00:24:18.956 --> 00:24:22.761
<i> These babies she's
 steamrolling could
 very well be hers.</i>

00:24:23.561 --> 00:24:25.597
<i> Not her problem.</i>

00:24:25.797 --> 00:24:29.768
<i> She just wants to add another
 100 eggs to the season total.</i>

00:24:36.207 --> 00:24:38.576 align:start position:0%
<i>Throughout the world, all
sea turtle mothers leave their</i>

00:24:38.609 --> 00:24:40.879
<i>babies to fend for themselves.</i>

00:24:43.781 --> 00:24:47.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> The little ones have to
 make a mad dash to the sea,</i>

00:24:48.119 --> 00:24:50.422
<i> across a killing field.</i>

00:24:55.893 --> 00:24:59.097
<i> No parental protection, and
 every predator on the beach</i>

00:24:59.130 --> 00:25:01.132
<i> gunning for them.</i>

00:25:06.237 --> 00:25:08.907 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> Their chances
 are one in 1,000.</i>

00:25:14.078 --> 00:25:17.682 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Any baby that survives
 the ordeal remains easy
 prey for ocean predators.</i>

00:25:21.218 --> 00:25:25.090
<i> It won't reach breeding
 age for another ten years.</i>

00:25:27.325 --> 00:25:29.928
<i>Sure she's not the cuddliest
mother but playing the numbers</i>

00:25:29.961 --> 00:25:33.064
<i> game isn't a bad bet.</i>

00:25:33.397 --> 00:25:37.202
<i> She could produce thousands
 of young in her lifetime.</i>

00:25:38.102 --> 00:25:41.372 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> If more than two of those
 survive long enough to breed,</i>

00:25:41.405 --> 00:25:43.241
<i> that's called winning.</i>

00:25:49.246 --> 00:25:51.215 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Our next weird
 creature is the envy of</i>

00:25:51.248 --> 00:25:53.084 line:0%
<i> pregnant women everywhere.</i>

00:25:54.285 --> 00:25:57.822 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> The giant sea horse is
 neither gigantic nor a horse.</i>

00:26:00.257 --> 00:26:03.862 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Instead, it's a foot-long
 fish that lives in the
 Pacific Ocean.</i>

00:26:05.663 --> 00:26:09.834 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> But its name isn't
 nearly as mixed up as
 the way it reproduces.</i>

00:26:10.668 --> 00:26:12.771
<i> It starts off simple.</i>

00:26:13.404 --> 00:26:15.707
<i> Boy meets girl,
 a brief courtship,</i>

00:26:17.408 --> 00:26:19.344
<i> tails intertwine.</i>

00:26:20.445 --> 00:26:23.915 align:start position:0%
<i>The newly minted couple
will stay together
throughout the breeding season.</i>

00:26:25.149 --> 00:26:28.353
<i> About that breeding, the
 female makes the eggs.</i>

00:26:30.554 --> 00:26:32.757 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> But instead of
 growing them inside her,</i>

00:26:32.790 --> 00:26:35.794
<i> or depositing them on the
 ocean floor like most fish,</i>

00:26:36.027 --> 00:26:38.697
<i> she deposits them in the guy.</i>

00:26:40.464 --> 00:26:44.502
<i> A specialized pouch
 in his belly opens up
 to receive the eggs.</i>

00:26:49.106 --> 00:26:51.109
<i> She floats away.</i>

00:26:51.409 --> 00:26:54.512 align:start position:0%
<i>He fertilizes the eggs and
takes over the heavy-duty work</i>

00:26:54.545 --> 00:26:57.916 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> of incubating their offspring
 over the next few weeks.</i>

00:26:59.116 --> 00:27:01.819
<i> Why does the male eat
 for several hundred?</i>

00:27:01.852 --> 00:27:05.090
<i> Reproduction is
 energy intensive.</i>

00:27:05.356 --> 00:27:07.425
<i> By sharing the baby burden,</i>

00:27:07.458 --> 00:27:09.460
<i> it gives the female
 a chance to invest her</i>

00:27:09.493 --> 00:27:12.464 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> energy in laying
 the next round of eggs.</i>

00:27:13.164 --> 00:27:16.167 line:0%
<i> More eggs means more chances
 some offspring will survive.</i>

00:27:20.271 --> 00:27:22.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> The father finds out
 the hard way when the young</i>

00:27:22.440 --> 00:27:24.075
<i> are ready to emerge.</i>

00:27:26.177 --> 00:27:28.246
<i> He experiences a set of
 intense contractions.</i>

00:27:29.480 --> 00:27:32.183 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> No lamaze
 classes for this guy.</i>

00:27:32.516 --> 00:27:34.419
<i> He just suffers through it.</i>

00:27:34.452 --> 00:27:37.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> And up to 400 children
 wriggle free and swim away.</i>

00:27:39.156 --> 00:27:43.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> And he looks for
 his mate to start the
 painful process over again.</i>

00:27:43.995 --> 00:27:46.164
<i> That's just mixed up.</i>

00:27:49.366 --> 00:27:51.970 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Parenting styles are as
 varied as in the human world.</i>

00:27:53.771 --> 00:27:56.574 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> You've got tiger moms,
 helicopter dads,</i>

00:27:58.976 --> 00:28:01.579
<i> the free-rangers,
 and worry warts.</i>

00:28:03.981 --> 00:28:06.417
<i> But when the only rule
 children have to obey is</i>

00:28:06.450 --> 00:28:09.154 align:start position:0%
<i>survival of the fittest, there
are bound to be problems.</i>

00:28:14.525 --> 00:28:17.629 align:start position:0%
<i>A pair of snowy egrets
makes a handsome young couple.</i>

00:28:18.529 --> 00:28:21.366 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> They're graceful,
 and elegantly dressed.</i>

00:28:24.301 --> 00:28:27.405 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> But this picture-perfect
 family hides a dirty
 little secret.</i>

00:28:32.209 --> 00:28:34.679
<i> A murder is about
 to be committed,</i>

00:28:34.712 --> 00:28:37.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> and nobody's
 ruffling a feather over it.</i>

00:28:41.318 --> 00:28:43.588 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Snowy egrets inhabit
 the waterways of the US,</i>

00:28:43.621 --> 00:28:45.690
<i> Central and South America.</i>

00:28:49.593 --> 00:28:52.464
<i> This pair in Florida have
 three little hatchlings.</i>

00:28:53.831 --> 00:28:56.501 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> They share the
 work of raising them.</i>

00:28:57.802 --> 00:29:00.939
<i> Taking turns, stalking
 the shallow salt marsh,</i>

00:29:03.207 --> 00:29:05.910 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> spearing small
 fish and crustaceans,</i>

00:29:06.343 --> 00:29:09.214
<i> and shuttling food
 back to the nest.</i>

00:29:09.847 --> 00:29:12.016 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> There's one thing that
 doesn't seem to concern them:</i>

00:29:14.485 --> 00:29:17.021
<i> it's what the kids
 are up to at home.</i>

00:29:20.724 --> 00:29:23.928
<i> The two oldest chicks
 are getting stronger
 and more aggressive.</i>

00:29:25.830 --> 00:29:28.366
<i> While the youngest
 only gets weaker.</i>

00:29:29.867 --> 00:29:33.071 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> At first the older chicks
 just shove it out of the way.</i>

00:29:33.871 --> 00:29:37.142 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i>But then they begin to stab and
beat their younger sibling.</i>

00:29:41.345 --> 00:29:43.581
(growl)

00:29:47.284 --> 00:29:49.087
<i> Mom's right there.</i>

00:29:49.787 --> 00:29:51.556
<i> Does she intervene?</i>

00:29:52.089 --> 00:29:55.193
<i> No, she turns a blind eye.</i>

00:29:57.595 --> 00:30:00.498 align:start position:0%
<i>As far as these parents are
concerned three chicks is more</i>

00:30:00.531 --> 00:30:02.901
<i> than they can feed this year.</i>

00:30:03.701 --> 00:30:07.071
<i> So they let the kids
 settle it themselves.</i>

00:30:09.773 --> 00:30:11.309
<i> The parents may not care,</i>

00:30:11.342 --> 00:30:14.045 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> but at least there's one
 bystander who does.</i>

00:30:20.784 --> 00:30:23.788
<i> The evidence is
 quickly erased.</i>

00:30:26.257 --> 00:30:28.827 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Mom and dad
 keep up appearances
 like nothing happened.</i>

00:30:30.461 --> 00:30:33.665
<i> A little family murder
 is swept under the rug.</i>

00:30:36.467 --> 00:30:38.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Bizarre behavior can strike
 some of the world's most</i>

00:30:38.736 --> 00:30:43.308 align:start position:0%
<i>famous mothers and fathers;
Antarctica's emperor penguins.</i>

00:30:45.910 --> 00:30:48.546 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Their dedication to
 their young is legendary.</i>

00:30:50.314 --> 00:30:52.717 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Almost immediately
 after laying the egg,</i>

00:30:52.750 --> 00:30:55.620 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> mother penguins march
 to the sea on a food run.</i>

00:30:57.554 --> 00:31:00.625
<i> While fathers endure the
 coldest winter on earth,</i>

00:31:01.025 --> 00:31:04.262 align:start position:0%
<i>incubating the pair's
precious egg until it hatches.</i>

00:31:06.330 --> 00:31:10.368
<i> It's a brutal three months,
 taking a toll on eggs and</i>

00:31:10.935 --> 00:31:13.037
<i> new-borns alike.</i>

00:31:15.539 --> 00:31:18.476
<i> Mothers return with bellies
 full of fish for their young.</i>

00:31:19.276 --> 00:31:23.381 align:start position:0%
<i>Unfortunately, they're also
carrying a recipe for madness.</i>

00:31:28.652 --> 00:31:31.923 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Their blood is
 coursing with prolactin;</i>

00:31:31.956 --> 00:31:34.825 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> a powerful hormone that
 stimulates parental behavior</i>

00:31:34.858 --> 00:31:36.895
<i> in both males and females.</i>

00:31:38.495 --> 00:31:41.799 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Most mothers reunite with
 their mate and instantly bond</i>

00:31:41.832 --> 00:31:45.103
<i> with a chick they've
 never seen before.</i>

00:31:45.903 --> 00:31:48.339
<i> But for those whose
 chicks have died,</i>

00:31:48.372 --> 00:31:50.408
<i> there's no reunion.</i>

00:31:50.875 --> 00:31:53.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Her parental
 hormones are still raging.</i>

00:31:54.245 --> 00:31:57.048 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> She searches the mob
 for a chick to nurture.</i>

00:31:57.081 --> 00:31:58.683
<i> Any chick.</i>

00:32:00.851 --> 00:32:02.820
<i> Even if it means kidnapping.</i>

00:32:04.288 --> 00:32:07.392
<i> The real parents fight to
 keep control of their baby.</i>

00:32:08.559 --> 00:32:10.962 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> In the melee a
 chick can be crushed,</i>

00:32:11.195 --> 00:32:13.598
<i> sometimes by its own
 mother and father.</i>

00:32:22.039 --> 00:32:24.342 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Occasionally the
 imposters win the battle.</i>

00:32:30.514 --> 00:32:32.817
<i> But the chick's unfamiliar
 call doesn't trigger their</i>

00:32:32.850 --> 00:32:35.086
<i> instinct to feed it.</i>

00:32:36.286 --> 00:32:38.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Once their madness
 passes, they lose interest.</i>

00:32:42.326 --> 00:32:44.662
<i> Leaving the chick
 hungry and alone.</i>

00:32:47.031 --> 00:32:49.767 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Where temperatures
 hover at 20 below zero,</i>

00:32:49.967 --> 00:32:52.704 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> injured chicks
 don't survive long.</i>

00:32:54.405 --> 00:32:57.808
<i>Nature's weirdest ironic twist
proves that you can have too</i>

00:32:57.841 --> 00:33:00.111
<i> much of a good thing.</i>

00:33:00.478 --> 00:33:04.916 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Even the most positive
 parental urges can
 have a sinister side.</i>

00:33:11.488 --> 00:33:14.225 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: The survival of
 the weird just got weirder.</i>

00:33:15.125 --> 00:33:17.195
<i> Meet the thresher shark.</i>

00:33:18.695 --> 00:33:22.500 align:start position:0%
<i>It may be one of the most
recognizable fish in the ocean.</i>

00:33:24.301 --> 00:33:26.938 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> The long tail propels it
 forward in perpetual motion.</i>

00:33:29.773 --> 00:33:32.309
<i> Sharks like the thresher are
 one of just a few kinds of</i>

00:33:32.342 --> 00:33:35.146
<i> animal that never
 come to a stop.</i>

00:33:38.048 --> 00:33:41.352 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> They are ram ventilators,
 meaning they can only breathe</i>

00:33:41.385 --> 00:33:43.354 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> as long as they
 are moving forward,</i>

00:33:43.620 --> 00:33:46.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> and water is
 flushing past their gills.</i>

00:33:49.393 --> 00:33:52.497
<i> For the thresher,
 to stop is to die.</i>

00:33:55.666 --> 00:33:58.669 align:start position:0%
<i>But the thresher shark's
enormously long whip-like tail</i>

00:33:58.702 --> 00:34:01.973 align:start position:0%
<i>is also put to work in the
world's weirdest shark attack.</i>

00:34:04.975 --> 00:34:07.545 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> This small-mouthed,
 small toothed shark hunts</i>

00:34:07.578 --> 00:34:10.515
<i> mostly small schooling fish.</i>

00:34:14.651 --> 00:34:17.655
<i>The shark's long tail provides
the speed and maneuverability</i>

00:34:17.688 --> 00:34:20.158
<i>necessary to chase these fish.</i>

00:34:21.592 --> 00:34:24.328
<i> When the thresher can find
 a tightly packed school,</i>

00:34:24.995 --> 00:34:26.964 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> it uses an extremely
 rare hunting technique,</i>

00:34:27.831 --> 00:34:29.967
<i> unique among sharks.</i>

00:34:40.878 --> 00:34:44.381 align:start position:0%
<i>It drives forward and down
flipping its tail over its head,</i>

00:34:44.414 --> 00:34:46.584
<i> and cracking it like a whip.</i>

00:34:58.896 --> 00:35:01.132 align:start position:0%
<i>The tip of the thresher's tail
has been measured moving at</i>

00:35:01.165 --> 00:35:04.035
<i> almost 50 miles an hour.</i>

00:35:06.570 --> 00:35:09.240
<i> It strikes with enough energy
 that several fish at a time</i>

00:35:09.273 --> 00:35:12.643 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> can be taken out with
 its high-speed tail slap.</i>

00:35:15.946 --> 00:35:19.316 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> The thresher's tail generates
 enough force to propel the</i>

00:35:19.349 --> 00:35:22.386 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> shark right out of
 the water if necessary.</i>

00:35:32.196 --> 00:35:35.199 align:start position:0%
<i>For small sharks and fish,
surviving a close call with an</i>

00:35:35.232 --> 00:35:37.368
<i> angel shark is a rare event.</i>

00:35:40.070 --> 00:35:43.407 align:start position:0%
<i>Angel sharks have fallen so
far from the shark family tree</i>

00:35:43.440 --> 00:35:46.611
<i> that they are virtually
 subterranean in lifestyle.</i>

00:35:55.152 --> 00:35:59.290
<i> But they may be the
 premier ambush hunters
 of the shark world.</i>

00:36:01.558 --> 00:36:06.531 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Unusual in sharks,
 the angel appears to be
 largely a visual hunter,</i>

00:36:07.498 --> 00:36:10.835 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> but one with weird
 and extreme capabilities.</i>

00:36:13.136 --> 00:36:17.408 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Angel sharks will
 settle to the bottom and
 gently bury themselves.</i>

00:36:18.208 --> 00:36:21.779 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Setting a trap of
 impressive proportions.</i>

00:36:23.013 --> 00:36:26.717 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
<i> They may wait days in
 this position for
 prey to pass overhead.</i>

00:36:31.488 --> 00:36:34.392
<i> Then this booby-trap of a
 shark erupts from the sand,</i>

00:36:34.692 --> 00:36:36.060
<i> and strikes!</i>

00:36:40.397 --> 00:36:44.502 align:start position:0%
<i>In just a tenth of a second it
can arch its body upward in a
lightning fast attack.</i>

00:36:54.778 --> 00:36:57.381
<i> They've been seen charging
 at anything that passes by.</i>

00:37:09.326 --> 00:37:12.763 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> They may spit the
 food out afterwards
 if they don't want it.</i>

00:37:12.796 --> 00:37:16.267
<i> A shark that has to wait for
 prey to pass overhead can't</i>

00:37:16.300 --> 00:37:18.102
<i> afford to be picky.</i>

00:37:24.374 --> 00:37:26.443
<i> The darkness of night isn't
 an obstacle for this shark's</i>

00:37:26.476 --> 00:37:28.479
<i> hair-trigger hunting style.</i>

00:37:29.580 --> 00:37:32.483
<i> But in a weird twist,
 it can't see in the dark</i>

00:37:32.516 --> 00:37:34.485
<i> like many night hunters can.</i>

00:37:35.452 --> 00:37:39.390 align:start position:0%
<i>Instead, the angel shark's
eyes appear to have evolved to</i>

00:37:39.423 --> 00:37:42.760 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> detect the faint glow of
 bioluminescent plankton that</i>

00:37:43.193 --> 00:37:45.396 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> will light up in the
 wake of a passing fish.</i>

00:37:46.763 --> 00:37:49.200
<i> A rare example of
 indirect detection.</i>

00:37:50.534 --> 00:37:53.203
<i> The angel shark can't
 see its prey at night,</i>

00:37:53.236 --> 00:37:55.739
<i> but it can detect the
 microscopic animals that</i>

00:37:55.772 --> 00:37:57.742
<i> detect its prey.</i>

00:37:59.043 --> 00:38:01.879 line:0%
<i> The angel shark's abilities
 are a stunning example of what</i>

00:38:01.912 --> 00:38:05.116 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
<i> hundreds of millions of years
 of trial and error can do.</i>

00:38:12.422 --> 00:38:15.159 line:0%
(howl)

00:38:15.192 --> 00:38:17.728 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: These are the
 survivalists of the wild.</i>

00:38:18.028 --> 00:38:22.233 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Preparing for the
 most extreme circumstances
 in the world's weirdest ways.</i>

00:38:24.067 --> 00:38:26.837
<i>Ready to hide, ready to fight.</i>

00:38:27.504 --> 00:38:30.241
<i> And in a losing battle,
 ready with an exit plan.</i>

00:38:33.076 --> 00:38:36.747 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> The North American
 bobcat is a hunter with
 a wide range of tastes.</i>

00:38:39.683 --> 00:38:44.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> It's looking for an easy
 meal and has this harmless
 hognose snake in its sights,</i>

00:38:48.458 --> 00:38:51.829 align:start position:0%
<i>but this little snake knows
how to act like it's dangerous;</i>

00:38:54.197 --> 00:38:58.836
<i> hissing, and flaring
 like a cobra's hood.</i>

00:39:02.038 --> 00:39:03.607
(hissing)

00:39:07.411 --> 00:39:10.414 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Seeming to be big
 and bad, often works.</i>

00:39:15.085 --> 00:39:18.055 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> But bobcats
 aren't easily fooled.</i>

00:39:24.628 --> 00:39:26.731 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> The snake's
 problem just got bigger,</i>

00:39:28.965 --> 00:39:32.503 align:start position:0%
<i>so the hognose must dig
deeper into its bag of tricks.</i>

00:39:37.007 --> 00:39:40.745
<i> With high drama,
 it plays dead.</i>

00:39:48.452 --> 00:39:52.690 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> It even exudes a
 rotting smell to kill
 the bobcat's curiosity.</i>

00:40:02.299 --> 00:40:05.936 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Great hunters like the
 bobcat prefer fresh meat,</i>

00:40:07.571 --> 00:40:12.877
<i> and little appetite for a
 dish of stinking dead snake.</i>

00:40:13.878 --> 00:40:18.315
<i>The snake knows this and gives
the performance of its life.</i>

00:40:18.515 --> 00:40:21.752 align:start position:0%
<i>When the bobcat gives up and
goes in search of a better meal,</i>

00:40:21.785 --> 00:40:24.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> the little
 mutant's problem is solved.</i>

00:40:33.396 --> 00:40:37.768 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> It takes a bow,
 and exits stage left.</i>

00:40:45.475 --> 00:40:49.246 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> The markets of
 Jaipur, India are under
 constant threat from bandits,</i>

00:40:52.716 --> 00:40:56.020 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> waiting for
 an unsuspecting target.</i>

00:41:00.223 --> 00:41:02.960
<i> This gang of langur
 monkeys is devious,</i>

00:41:02.993 --> 00:41:05.763
<i> relentless and worst
 of all, untouchable.</i>

00:41:09.799 --> 00:41:13.003
<i> Monkeys are symbols
 of the Hindu gods.</i>

00:41:13.603 --> 00:41:16.574
<i> Harming them is a
 religious offense.</i>

00:41:17.041 --> 00:41:19.777
<i> The most the fruit seller
 can do is shoo them away.</i>

00:41:24.881 --> 00:41:27.251 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> The monkey's biggest
 threat comes from each other.</i>

00:41:28.952 --> 00:41:32.456 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> They form rival gangs, roaming
 the streets and fighting</i>

00:41:32.489 --> 00:41:35.659
<i> turf wars over access to
 the ample supply of food.</i>

00:41:36.726 --> 00:41:38.862
<i> As India becomes
 more urbanized,</i>

00:41:38.895 --> 00:41:41.966
<i> expect more monkey mafias.</i>

00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:45.936
<i> An unstoppable menace.</i>

00:41:45.969 --> 00:41:48.806
<i> But one that can
 be weirdly cute.</i>

00:41:54.044 --> 00:41:56.847 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Autumn leaves are
 already starting to fall,</i>

00:41:57.881 --> 00:42:01.685 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> and with them, the
 last morsels of food.</i>

00:42:04.554 --> 00:42:06.790
<i> Now is the time for grey
 squirrels to put their</i>

00:42:06.823 --> 00:42:09.193
<i> emergency plan into action,</i>

00:42:09.927 --> 00:42:12.530 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> storing away protein-rich
 nuts for winter.</i>

00:42:13.830 --> 00:42:16.600
<i> It seems like an
 innocent activity,</i>

00:42:16.866 --> 00:42:19.236
<i> but what's astonishing
 about these hoarders,</i>

00:42:19.269 --> 00:42:21.605 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> is their devious,</i> 
<i> tactical mind.</i>

00:42:24.074 --> 00:42:26.410
<i> They're well versed in
 the art of espionage.</i>

00:42:29.145 --> 00:42:31.482
<i> It's the acorn cold war.</i>

00:42:32.949 --> 00:42:35.719 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> A stealthy spy
 watches from above,</i>

00:42:37.220 --> 00:42:39.990 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> waiting for a squirrel to
 reveal her nut hiding spot so</i>

00:42:40.023 --> 00:42:42.226
<i> he can steal it for himself.</i>

00:42:44.127 --> 00:42:46.096
<i> But he's been busted.</i>

00:42:46.129 --> 00:42:48.566
<i> The squirrel on the ground
 knows she's being watched.</i>

00:42:49.366 --> 00:42:51.602
<i> And she puts on a show.</i>

00:42:53.637 --> 00:42:56.807
<i> She digs a hole,
 as usual, but,</i>

00:42:56.840 --> 00:42:58.508
<i>with a little sleight of hand,</i>

00:42:58.541 --> 00:43:00.844 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> she escapes
 without burying anything.</i>

00:43:08.785 --> 00:43:13.157
<i> The spy swoops in,
 and he's been duped.</i>

00:43:15.191 --> 00:43:17.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> The nut has already been
 squirreled away to another,</i>

00:43:17.727 --> 00:43:19.997
<i> more secret location.</i>

00:43:24.534 --> 00:43:28.172 align:start position:0%
<i>It's hard enough to keep track
of hundreds of buried nuts.</i>

00:43:29.206 --> 00:43:32.810
<i> Much harder when nature
 covers it all in white.</i>

00:43:33.877 --> 00:43:37.348 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> But the squirrel is a
 master of mental gymnastics.</i>

00:43:38.449 --> 00:43:41.785 line:0%
<i> It remembers landmarks,
 like trees and buildings,</i>

00:43:41.818 --> 00:43:45.489 line:0%
<i> and triangulates a mental
 map of its hidden stashes.</i>

00:43:47.090 --> 00:43:49.626 line:0%
<i> It's believed that squirrels
 can locate a nut up to nine</i>

00:43:49.659 --> 00:43:52.396 line:0%
<i> months after it was buried!</i>

00:43:55.565 --> 00:43:57.868 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
<i> With not only
 phenomenal memory,</i>

00:43:57.901 --> 00:44:02.539 line:0%
<i> but the ability to deceive,
 the remarkable grey squirrel</i>

00:44:03.172 --> 00:44:07.177 line:0%
<i> is a forward thinker,
 with a license to live.</i>

00:44:09.379 --> 00:44:10.581 line:0%
Captioned by Cotter
Captioning Services.

00:44:10.914 --> 00:44:11.982 line:0%
 

